Plan Code:

731
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:27,670
G-B-A-C-K.

732
00:15:27,670 --> 00:15:29,710
I call it G-Back!

733
00:15:31,500 --> 00:15:33,670
That sounds pretty amazing!

734
00:15:33,670 --> 00:15:35,300
This'll be fun.

735
00:15:35,300 --> 00:15:37,880
You say that now,

736
00:15:38,300 --> 00:15:43,770
but when this plan explodes, you may not survive.

737
00:15:44,850 --> 00:15:46,690
You're serious. Aren't you, Kyouma?

738
00:15:47,030 --> 00:15:48,650
Let's make this clear:

739
00:15:48,650 --> 00:15:52,980
If I participate, you tell me everything.

740
00:15:53,360 --> 00:15:54,320
Understood?

741
00:15:54,690 --> 00:15:56,650
The cat ears never lie.

742
00:15:57,030 --> 00:15:57,610
I'll teach you...

743
00:15:57,610 --> 00:16:01,030
...that you just can't beat some opponents!

744
00:16:01,930 --> 00:16:02,620
I lose!

745
00:16:02,620 --> 00:16:03,080
Fast!

746
00:16:03,080 --> 00:16:05,620
Mayushii is disappointed.

747
00:16:05,620 --> 00:16:07,580
What was your plan?

748
00:16:07,580 --> 00:16:08,500
Who knows?

749
00:16:08,790 --> 00:16:12,920
But he just kept charging me, like he was self-destructing.

750
00:16:13,300 --> 00:16:14,500
Jibaku?

751
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:17,260
G-Back... G-Back?

752
00:16:17,260 --> 00:16:19,840
That was a horrible joke, thank you very much.

753
00:16:19,840 --> 00:16:20,390
However!

754
00:16:20,390 --> 00:16:21,220
What?

755
00:16:21,220 --> 00:16:23,220
Tell me what you know, Feyris.

756
00:16:21,470 --> 00:16:23,220
He recovers quickly.

757
00:16:23,640 --> 00:16:25,520
For a loser, you're arrogant.

758
00:16:26,180 --> 00:16:30,230
I said if I participated, you'd tell me what you know.

759
00:16:30,230 --> 00:16:34,270
In other words, I never cared about winning.

760
00:16:34,270 --> 00:16:35,070
Is that right?

761
00:16:35,480 --> 00:16:37,150
I don't really remember...

762
00:16:37,150 --> 00:16:38,200
Remember it!

763
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:39,780
It was my brilliant plan!

764
00:16:39,990 --> 00:16:42,740
Brilliant or cheating, one of the two.

765
00:16:42,740 --> 00:16:43,580
Shut up!

766
00:16:43,580 --> 00:16:45,990
Where's the IBN 5100?

767
00:16:45,990 --> 00:16:47,160
I don't know...

768
00:16:47,160 --> 00:16:48,410
You don't know?

769
00:16:48,410 --> 00:16:54,250
I'm sure when I was little, Dad had one, but it's gone.

770
00:16:54,610 --> 00:16:55,800
Why, you...

771
00:16:55,800 --> 00:16:57,050
Is that the secret move

772
00:16:57,050 --> 00:17:00,380
you mastered in the Guiana Highlands, the Question-Dodge?

773
00:17:00,380 --> 00:17:01,840
How did you know?

774
00:17:02,590 --> 00:17:04,010
Way to go, Kyouma.

775
00:17:04,430 --> 00:17:07,390
You saw through my Ignoring Shoulder.

776
00:17:11,020 --> 00:17:12,270
Is that really it?

777
00:17:12,650 --> 00:17:13,860
Yeah.

778
00:17:13,860 --> 00:17:17,480
I'm pretty sure the last time I saw it was at an Akihabara shrine.

779
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:19,320
Shrine?

780
00:17:20,110 --> 00:17:21,110
"Kurisu,

781
00:17:21,110 --> 00:17:23,200
Thank you for messaging us all the way from Japan."

782
00:17:23,740 --> 00:17:27,660
"About your question, I asked the professor,

783
00:17:27,660 --> 00:17:29,960
and he said that yes, the IBN 5100

784
00:17:29,960 --> 00:17:34,790
can analyze certain special programming languages."

785
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:36,460
He was serious?

786
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:44,430
A computer?

787
00:17:44,430 --> 00:17:46,430
I'll have to ask my father.

788
00:17:46,720 --> 00:17:48,770
An IBN 5100.

789
00:17:48,770 --> 00:17:51,690
If he doesn't know what that is, tell him it's an old computer.

790
00:17:51,690 --> 00:17:52,770
All right.

791
00:17:52,770 --> 00:17:53,770
I'll ask him.

792
00:17:53,770 --> 00:17:54,400
I'm counting on you.

793
00:17:54,810 --> 00:17:56,440
End with the code words.

794
00:17:56,440 --> 00:17:59,190
E-El... Psy Congri...

795
00:17:59,570 --> 00:18:00,490
It's Congroo!

796
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:05,120
Hello?

797
00:18:05,550 --> 00:18:06,740
It's Makise.

798
00:18:06,740 --> 00:18:08,200
Makise?

799
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:09,870
Sorry, I don't remember any Makise's.

800
00:18:09,870 --> 00:18:11,040
Where did we meet?

801
00:18:11,040 --> 00:18:12,500
Paris? London?

802
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:13,790
Akihabara.

803
00:18:13,790 --> 00:18:15,130
I just saw you!

804
00:18:15,130 --> 00:18:17,500
What? It's my assistant?

805
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:19,840
Just say "Christina"!

806
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:20,960
There's no -tina!

807
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:23,340
You're as loud and bossy as ever.

808
00:18:23,340 --> 00:18:24,970
Whose fault is that? Whose?

809
00:18:25,510 --> 00:18:26,640
What do you want?

810
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:28,390
Where are you now?

811
00:18:28,640 --> 00:18:29,760
Why do you care?

812
00:18:29,760 --> 00:18:30,720
No reason.

813
00:18:31,430 --> 00:18:34,060
I'm heading to Yanabayashi Shrine...

814
00:18:36,060 --> 00:18:37,190
What was that?

815
00:18:37,190 --> 00:18:38,190
Harassment?

816
00:18:38,190 --> 00:18:39,690
Was that harassment?

817
00:18:40,530 --> 00:18:42,190
What was that call about?

818
00:18:42,190 --> 00:18:44,360
I just asked where you were.

819
00:18:44,360 --> 00:18:46,280
No one called you.

820
00:18:46,660 --> 00:18:48,830
No one called me.

821
00:18:50,370 --> 00:18:52,040
I'm back!

822
00:18:52,620 --> 00:18:53,660
Did you ask him?

823
00:18:53,660 --> 00:18:59,340
Yes, he said that we have that PC here.

824
00:18:59,340 --> 00:19:00,210
Really?

825
00:19:00,210 --> 00:19:01,380
PC?

826
00:19:01,760 --> 00:19:03,760
Do you mean an IBN 5100?

827
00:19:04,340 --> 00:19:05,300
Yes.

828
00:19:05,300 --> 00:19:07,300
Um, who is this?

829
00:19:07,300 --> 00:19:08,180
My assistant.

830
00:19:08,180 --> 00:19:09,180
Anyway, the IBNâ

831
00:19:09,180 --> 00:19:10,310
Wait!

832
00:19:10,310 --> 00:19:12,680
What kind of introduction is that?

833
00:19:13,140 --> 00:19:15,440
And I'm not your assistant!

834
00:19:15,440 --> 00:19:18,770
I'm not here to introduce you.

835
00:19:18,770 --> 00:19:20,860
It wouldn't even take ten seconds.

836
00:19:21,230 --> 00:19:23,190
You're a pain, you know that?

837
00:19:23,490 --> 00:19:25,360
Makise Kurisu, my assistant.

838
00:19:25,360 --> 00:19:26,530
Right, right.

839
00:19:26,530 --> 00:19:28,370
Fine, I'm your assistant.

840
00:19:28,370 --> 00:19:29,370
So who are you?

841
00:19:29,780 --> 00:19:31,700
U-Urushibara Ruka.

842
00:19:32,080 --> 00:19:33,240
How old are you?

843
00:19:33,240 --> 00:19:35,460
Seventeen this year.

844
00:19:35,460 --> 00:19:36,830
One year younger than I am.

845
00:19:37,330 --> 00:19:38,540
Am I?

846
00:19:38,960 --> 00:19:41,540
You look like a grown-up, Makise-san.

847
00:19:41,540 --> 00:19:42,420
You're pretty.

848
00:19:42,420 --> 00:19:44,880
No... Not nearly as pretty as you.

849
00:19:45,800 --> 00:19:48,550
Um... I'll call my dad.

850
00:19:49,760 --> 00:19:51,390
Some things it's better not to know, huh?

851
00:19:51,760 --> 00:19:52,810
What do you mean?

852
00:19:54,720 --> 00:19:58,770
I never thought it would happen.

853
00:19:58,770 --> 00:20:00,900
Wh-What do you mean?

854
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:04,570
Um, well, the person who donated this told us...

855
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:09,160
that someday, a young man would appear who needed it.

856
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:11,240
So take good care of it.

857
00:20:11,620 --> 00:20:14,120
It was ten years ago, I think?

858
00:20:14,540 --> 00:20:16,370
So that's it...

859
00:20:16,870 --> 00:20:18,500
It's fate.

860
00:20:19,020 --> 00:20:20,830
The choice of Steins Gate!

861
00:20:20,830 --> 00:20:22,090
That again?

862
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:31,680
IBN 5100 Portable Computer.

863
00:20:32,430 --> 00:20:33,560
This is it.

864
00:20:33,930 --> 00:20:36,140
Is that right?

865
00:20:36,140 --> 00:20:38,640
Um, could we borrow it?

866
00:20:38,640 --> 00:20:39,350
Certainly.

867
00:20:40,770 --> 00:20:41,730
Thank you.

868
00:20:42,150 --> 00:20:43,190
We're carrying this back! Help me!

869
00:20:43,190 --> 00:20:44,150
But I refuse.

870
00:20:44,150 --> 00:20:45,980
You're my assistant, Christina!

871
00:20:45,980 --> 00:20:47,990
I'm not your assistant, and there's no -tina!

872
00:20:49,030 --> 00:20:50,740
I'll get a cart.

873
00:20:51,780 --> 00:20:54,660
We couldn't ask you for that, after you lent this to us.

874
00:20:54,660 --> 00:20:55,740
Hey, assistant!

875
00:20:55,740 --> 00:20:57,290
Show some respect for others!

876
00:20:58,790 --> 00:21:00,580
Show some respect?

877
00:21:00,580 --> 00:21:01,620
You really just said that?

878
00:21:02,670 --> 00:21:04,130
You guys are good friends, huh?

879
00:21:04,710 --> 00:21:07,340
Be nice to Ruka, too.

880
00:21:07,340 --> 00:21:07,840
Yes, please.

881
00:21:09,540 --> 00:21:11,680
Wait just a moment.

882
00:21:14,100 --> 00:21:15,680
You have a nice father.

883
00:21:16,410 --> 00:21:17,470
You think so?

884
00:21:18,060 --> 00:21:20,730
<i>I don't want to make the same mistake as my father!</i>

885
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:24,230
What?

886
00:21:24,650 --> 00:21:25,570
Nothing.

887
00:21:26,690 --> 00:21:28,070
I'm sorry!

888
00:21:28,070 --> 00:21:31,030
The cart is broken.

889
00:21:34,200 --> 00:21:36,830
Why do I have to do this with you?

890
00:21:36,830 --> 00:21:38,080
Shut up and carry it.

891
00:21:38,080 --> 00:21:39,580
We've got a long way to go.

892
00:21:44,330 --> 00:21:45,040
Hey...

893
00:21:45,040 --> 00:21:45,960
What?

894
00:21:45,960 --> 00:21:47,050
It's nothing!

895
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:50,760
What's with your provocations?

896
00:21:51,880 --> 00:21:53,180
Wait!

897
00:21:53,180 --> 00:21:54,720
If you carry it like that, I'll have to walk backwards!

898
00:21:54,720 --> 00:21:56,910
Start walking, assistant!

899
00:21:57,570 --> 00:21:58,640
I can't...

900
